      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8d442bc4",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: dick_punch_bear_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two bears play-fighting in water, with the text 'dick punch' and 'funny regardless of species'. The meme uses a crude, vulgar pun ('dick punch') to describe a physical interaction between animals, which is inherently offensive and degrading. While the image itself does not target a specific human group, the use of vulgar language and the implication of sexualized violence (even if metaphorical) can be considered harmful due to its crude nature and potential to offend viewers. The intent is to create humor through shock value and crude wordplay, which may be seen as inappropriate or offensive in many contexts, especially when juxtaposed with the natural behavior of animals. The meme does not contain direct hate or abuse toward any protected group, but its crude and vulgar content can be considered harmful due to its potential to cause offense or discomfort.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8e68bb12"
